@startuml hld-04b_engine_track_schedule
title HLD-04b — The Engine track, DETAIL (UML **package diagram**)\nEvery element, where it is built, and the «trace» that lifts it into the Engine at step E0–E3 (§8.4).\nThe three zones and the lift precondition are HLD-04a.
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 210
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide circle

package "sagittarius_engine as it stands today" <<Framework 2.4.0>> #WhiteSmoke {
  class IExtension <<interface>>
  class ExtensionDescriptor
  class ExtensionManager
  class IContainer <<interface>>
  class IEventBus <<interface>>
  class QtEventBridge
  class IDispatcher <<interface>>
  class Scheduler
  class HostedServiceManager
  class PresenterManager
  class create_quick_widget <<function>>
}

package "application :: lift-ready staging area  (Phase 0–1)" <<harvest zone>> #LightYellow {
  class BoundedContextModule <<abstract>>
  class IContributionRegistry <<interface>>
  class ContributionDescriptor <<frozen dataclass>>
  class Place <<enumeration>>
  class SizeHint <<enumeration>>
  class Surface
  class NavigationPolicy
}

package "sagittarius_engine :: extensions::workbench  (target)" <<lifted>> #LightGreen {
  class WorkbenchModule <<abstract>> {
    **E1** — after app Phase 1
    (two surfaces, two modules exist)
  }
  class ContributionRegistry {
    **E1**
  }
  class RegionHost {
    **E2** — after app Phase 2
    (strategy contributes into backtest)
  }
  class NavigationService {
    **E3** — app Phase 5
    USER_INTENT vs RESTORE · can_leave
  }
  class ScheduledJobCancel <<operation>> {
    **E0** — now, independent of the app
  }
  class QuickWidgetImportPaths <<operation>> {
    **E3** — when ADR D6 reopens
  }
}

package "application :: policy" <<never moves>> #LightGray {
  class ModuleList
  class SurfaceCatalog
  class DevModeGate
  class BinanceGateway
}

IExtension <|-- BoundedContextModule
BoundedContextModule ..> QtEventBridge : <<use>>
IContributionRegistry ..> IContainer : <<use>>
Surface ..> PresenterManager : <<use>>
NavigationPolicy ..> PresenterManager : <<use>>

BoundedContextModule ..> WorkbenchModule : <<trace>> E1
IContributionRegistry ..> ContributionRegistry : <<trace>> E1
ContributionDescriptor ..> ContributionRegistry : <<trace>> E1
Place ..> ContributionRegistry : <<trace>> E1
SizeHint ..> ContributionRegistry : <<trace>> E1
Surface ..> RegionHost : <<trace>> E2
NavigationPolicy ..> NavigationService : <<trace>> E3
Scheduler ..> ScheduledJobCancel : <<trace>> E0
create_quick_widget ..> QuickWidgetImportPaths : <<trace>> E3

ModuleList ..> BoundedContextModule : <<use>>
SurfaceCatalog ..> Surface : <<use>>

note bottom of BoundedContextModule
  **Three constraints that make each «trace» cheap, enforced from Phase 0 (§8.2):**
  1. no import from `modules`, `support` or the rest of `shell` — the Engine and
     the standard library only (`core` already carries this guard);
  2. Engine package layout — `core/contracts/contribution.py` is written as the future
     `sagittarius_engine/extensions/workbench/contribution.py`;
  3. the application subclasses a lift-bound type only through the intended seam —
     a module subclasses `BoundedContextModule`, and nothing else touches its internals.
end note

note right of NavigationService
  §5.3 said `contribute` / `subscribe` stay in the application "until a second
  application needs them". Under the harvest rule the second *surface* in this
  application is already enough evidence, so they lift at **E1**.
  §5.3 is superseded by §8.3.
end note

note bottom of DevModeGate
  These four never carry a «trace». The Engine must not learn *which* surfaces
  this application has — only *how* a surface is contributed to.
end note
@enduml
